      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that Dobbs is just \"originalism\" is a deliberate legal fiction because the Court ignored the clear, binding precedent set by *Roe* and *Casey* for fifty years that had already defined the right.\nIf they truly believed they were just following the text, they would have acknowledged that the Constitution's text was already interpreted as protecting abortion rights by the very justices who wrote those precedents.\nInstead, they used a narrow reading of the text to overturn decades of settled law, which proves the decision was a political choice to roll back fundamental rights rather than a neutral legal interpretation.\nThis isn't a new way of reading the text; it's a strategic move to erase the protections that were already firmly established in American jurisprudence.",
